WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.120
Canadian investors with energy or transport exposure could see margin pressure as diesel crosses $6 per gallon for the first time. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 169. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:56.820
The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,657, up 0.9%. The NASDAQ composite closed at 26,333, up 1%. The TSX composite closed at 35,698, up 0.5%. Core PCE projections for August sit between 0.25% and 0.28%.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:06.880
JP Morgan now sees two Fed rate hikes in its revised outlook. The nearest central bank decisions remain the Fed and Bank of Canada meetings later this month.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:22.700
Value investing focuses on stocks trading at low multiples of earnings, cash flow, or book value relative to historical norms or peers. Rising bond yields have started to challenge high valuation growth names that dominated the past two years.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:37.880
This shift creates a window where depressed multiples can act as a buffer against further drawdowns. Investors can screen for names with forward price to earnings ratios below sector mediums and free cash flow yields above 6%.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:51.700
Free tools on most Canadian broker platforms make that screen available in minutes. The approach has historically delivered its strongest relative performance in the 12 to 24 months after the 10 year treasury yield breaks above 4%.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:57.920
The main risk is value traps where companies look cheap only because earnings are about to fall.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:14.280
Pair any screen with the same day volume check above the 20-day average before entering. Canadian investors can run the same screen inside a TFSA by sorting TSX names on dividend yield and payout ratio while excluding recent earnings misses.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:27.240
The end of the lazy trade in growth stocks is opening space for buyers who focus on balance sheet strength. Imagine you bought XIU last month because it felt familiar and offered a dividend tax credit.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:34.840
Your order filled at the TSX close but the ETF carries a 30% plus weighting in financials and energy.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:45.640
Bat concentration means your Canada bet is really a sector bet that can lag global tech and health care for years. Canada represents roughly 3% of global market cap.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:56.380
Many TFSA and RRSP holders still keep 30 to 50% of equity exposure inside Canadian names due to familiarity and the dividend tax credit.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:04.900
Job, home and pension already deliver heavy Canada exposure so the extra allocation often doubles down on the same risks.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:11.540
Professionals check their total geographic breakdown across all accounts before adding another Canadian ETF.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:21.260
Calculate your true country weights once a quarter and cap Canadian equity at 20-25% unless you have a specific thesis for outperformance.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:27.560
That quarterly check can be completed in under 10 minutes using any brokerage portfolio analyzer.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.500
This week's practice investment remains in observation mode with no new entry.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:38.160
Kroger posted a second quarter earnings beat and the stock moved higher immediately afterward.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:45.380
The move has not yet produced volume above the 20-day average. RSI sits near 55 on the daily chart.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:53.040
The recent regime shows a median matched window alpha of negative 1.76% across the last 10 trades.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:58.840
Entry requires three aligned factors and only the earnings beat is confirmed so far.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:04.440
The invalidation remains a close below the 50-day moving average on above average volume.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:11.800
The setup shows how to stay disciplined during a cold streak by naming the exact missing conditions rather than forcing a trade.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:18.580
Preserving capital is an active decision, not a default. No newly closed trade since the last review.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:22.760
Current holdings remain open and pending their scheduled evaluation.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:35.540
The iShares S&amp;P TSX60 index ETF provides broad Canadian large cap exposure and can serve as a core holding for investors who want to benchmark their TSX allocation.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:44.180
Canadian investors can use the Outlook to compare sector weights against their own TFSA holdings and decide whether to add or trim.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:50.600
Access the latest commentary directly on the Kalkine site or through any brokerage research portal.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:58.920
The Outlook also flags upcoming corporate actions and dividend dates that can affect rebalancing decisions inside registered accounts.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:07.520
Investors who hold the ETF can cross reference its top holdings against recent Canadian names to avoid unintended concentration.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:14.260
Kroger posted second quarter results that beat expectations and the stock moved higher immediately afterward.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:21.000
The reaction was positive enough to prompt fresh questions about whether the valuation now justifies a new position.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:27.920
Add KR to the watch list and wait for volume above the 20-day average before considering any position.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.600
Three popular ETFs can still overlap heavily in US mega-cap tech names.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:39.420
The overlap leaves investors with unintended concentration even when they hold multiple funds.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:46.540
Run a holdings overlap check on your TFSA ETFs this week using your broker portfolio analyzer.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:53.460
Four Canadian stocks offering reliable income plus capital gains potential were highlighted for tax-free accounts.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:06:03.020
The selection criteria emphasize dividend growth history and balance sheet resilience that can compound inside a TFSA over multi-year periods.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:08.940
Review the four names against your existing TFSA sector weights before adding any new positions.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:16.860
Patient ownership of quality Canadian companies has compounded meaningfully inside registered accounts over multi-year periods.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:25.580
Consistent dividend reinvestment and modest annual contributions can produce outsized results when the holding period stretches beyond five years.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:36.860
Identify one Canadian stock already in your TFSA that has raised its dividend at least three times in the past five years and set a price alert at its 200-day moving average.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:46.800
Portfolio performance stands at 60 total trades with a 52% win rate for a cumulative P&amp;L of $299.63.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:54.720
The matched window alpha versus NASDAQ stands at negative 4.8% across nine rules-based trades.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:07:05.340
Average return per trade is 0.50% with the best trade at 20.11% and the worst at negative 11.80%.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:18.680
The current streak is one loss. These figures reflect the strict five session hold rule and the requirement that every trade be sized at exactly $1,000 with no discretionary extension of the holding period.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:33.820
Open your brokerage app, pull up the three largest ETFs in your TFSA and run the holdings overlap report. Note the combined weight in the top 10 US tech names and decide whether that concentration matches your intended risk level.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:48.080
Looking back over the past week, TFSA concentration risks remain front of mind as many holders still carry 30-50% Canadian equity despite the country representing only 3% of global market cap.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:58.180
Energy price shocks have intensified with diesel crossing the $6 threshold adding direct margin pressure to logistics and transport names on both sides of the border.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:11.560
Bank of Canada and Fed policy expectations continue to shift as core PCE projections stay in the 0.25 to 0.28% range and markets now price two potential Fed hikes.

